Individual-card N512 matched-seed follow-up to successful 5-for-5 N1024 ramp experiment.
Same deck engine, same action implementations, beam 240 and v0.77 inherited mulligan policy.
Six independent variants each run 512 games on game IDs 0..511, allowing paired outcomes.
Five single-card substitutions:
0: The One Ring -> Coalition Relic
1: Throne of Eldraine -> Implements of Sacrifice
2: Staff of Compleation -> Tooth of Ramos
3: Mirage Mirror -> Everflowing Chalice
4: Rings of Brighthearth -> Bucknard's Everfull Purse
Baseline: unchanged legal 99-card flicker deck.
Produces paired per-card marginal T1, T2 and T3 improvements and 95% confidence intervals.
Caution: individual effects may be nonadditive and do not include protection/interaction utility.
